        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-conus-audit-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-conus-audit-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-conus-audit-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-6>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-conus-audit-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-7> ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Elementary Cellular Automata (GF(2)) & Reaction-Diffusion PDE" ;
    pk:weightOfEvidence 8.73e-01 .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-conus-audit-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Wolfram (1984) Rule 30 & Meinhardt–Klingler (1987) Conus textile Pigmentation — Code-to-model traceability: 89/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "All figure titles, legends, and annotations in both 6-panel figures are dynamically formatted from the dictionary returned by `self_test()`, preventing hardcoded label drift between computed metrics and plotted text. Evidence: 1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py L973–L1148: render_comparison_figure(): dynamic formatting of all 6 panels from self_test() results <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fb234bc/1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py#L973-L1148>; 1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py L1285–L1504: render_kymograph_defect_front_figure(): dynamic formatting of dislocation indices, velocities, and sorting/bioelectric fronts <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fb234bc/1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py#L1285-L1504>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-code-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-conus-audit-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Wolfram (1984) Rule 30 & Meinhardt–Klingler (1987) Conus textile Pigmentation — Model fidelity to source: 89/100" ;
    dct:references <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-3> ;
    rdfs:comment "Implements both the discrete Wolfram Rule 30 cellular automaton (in both Boolean XOR/OR and GF(2) Algebraic Normal Form) and the continuous Meinhardt-Klingler (1987) 3-species activator-substrate-hormone mantle-edge PDE, plus Erica Jen's (1990) left-bijective spatial inverse, left-cone diagonal recursion d_k(t+1) = d_{k-2}(t) XOR (d_{k-1}(t) OR d_k(t)), and asymmetric Boolean Jacobian damage-cone analysis. Evidence: 1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py L140–L273: Rule 30 Boolean/ANF steppers, Jen (1990) left-bijective inverse, and Prize #1-#3 diagnostics <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fb234bc/1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py#L140-L273>; 1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py L276–L422: GF(2) Boolean Jacobian verification, diagonal period-doubling cascade k=0..414, and damage-cone ensemble <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fb234bc/1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py#L276-L422>; 1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py L627–L704: Meinhardt-Klingler (1987) activator-substrate-hormone PDE and 3D Raup Conus shell mesh <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fb234bc/1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py#L627-L704>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-conus-audit-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Wolfram (1984) Rule 30 & Meinhardt–Klingler (1987) Conus textile Pigmentation — Morphometric validation: 88/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Seven quantitative morphometrics and algebraic invariants are verified in `self_test()` and exported to `conus_textile_rule30_metrics.csv` and `conus_rule30_defect_fronts.csv`: 128/128 OEIS A051023 bit match, 0 bit errors on Jen's left-bijective inverse and diagonal recursion, exact dislocation indices k in {0, 3, 8, 29, 400}, damage-cone velocities v_R = +1.0000 and v_L = -0.2604, shell H/W = 1.8342 (ref 1.8330), silhouette IoU = 0.8353, and white-chord CV = 0.7069 (theory 1/sqrt(2) = 0.7071, specimen 0.6403). Evidence: 1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py L799–L913: self_test(): 9 automated assertion blocks covering algebraic, statistical, and geometric metrics <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fb234bc/1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py#L799-L913>; conus_textile_rule30_metrics.csv (generated output, not in repo): System-by-system pigment fraction, white-chord mean/CV, KS distance, fractal dimension, and silhouette IoU — conus_textile_rule30_metrics.csv: rendered output of 1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py at fb234bc, text/csv, 644 B, artifact_sha256 da34a299061268e937c073cc835a76f836bf1d976c145e9484147e922e21fa19 (sha256 da34a299061268e937c073cc835a76f836bf1d976c145e9484147e922e21fa19), spec_fingerprint 6baf9ffa515c0c89775df3b58f398571f7894e64d20534778dff610ad08bc313; conus_rule30_defect_fronts.csv (generated output, not in repo): 17 defect-front and dislocation rows across Rule 30, Meinhardt PDE, sorting, and bioelectricity — conus_rule30_defect_fronts.csv: rendered output of 1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py at fb234bc, text/csv, 1205 B, artifact_sha256 ed19157163ba7735b0da73a0e2cdc62d033a33f081266bf02a5da02f82f5af02 (sha256 ed19157163ba7735b0da73a0e2cdc62d033a33f081266bf02a5da02f82f5af02), spec_fingerprint 6baf9ffa515c0c89775df3b58f398571f7894e64d20534778dff610ad08bc313. Measurements (measure_outputs.py): Rule 30 center-column exact match to OEIS A051023 (first 128 bits) = 128 bits matched (reference 128, Wolfram 1984 Nature 311:419 / OEIS A051023 / Rule 30 Prize (2019)) [exact bitwise comparison of a_{t,0} (t=0..127) against OEIS A051023]; Jen (1990) left-bijective inverse & diagonal recursion bit errors = 0 bit errors (reference 0, Jen 1990 Physica D 45:3-18 Theorem 1 & Section 2) [sum of bit reconstruction errors across a_{t,i-1} = a_{t+1,i} XOR (a_{t,i} OR a_{t,i+1}) and d_k(t+1) = d_{k-2}(t) XOR (d_{k-1}(t) OR d_k(t))] — first 5 period-doubling dislocation diagonals k = [0, 3, 8, 29, 400] (P = 1, 2, 4, 8, 16); Rule 30 Prize #2 center-column density c_1024 = 0.4785 fraction of 1s (reference 0.5, Wolfram 2019 Rule 30 Prize Problem 2 (https://rule30prize.org/)) [cumulative fraction (1/N) sum_{t=0}^{1023} a_{t,0} on single-seed light-cone] — normalized 4-bit block Shannon entropy H_4/4 = 0.99640 bits/bit; left-cone periodic crystal lock-in front velocity v_lock = -0.1962 cells/step (reference -0.2081, Jen 1990 Physica D 45:3-18 / Wolfram 2002 A New Kind of Science p. 871) [spatial drift velocity of period-locked diagonal boundary (1/slope - 1 from T_lock(k) = 1.2441*k + 7.89 over k in [30, 400])] — damage-cone velocities: v_R = +1.0000±0.0000, v_L = -0.2604±0.1024 cells/step; 3D Raup Conus textile shell height-to-width ratio (H/W) = 1.8342 ratio (H/W) (reference 1.833, Conus textile OSU specimen 24399204286 (James St. John, CC BY 2.0)) [projected axial height / maximum shoulder diameter of 3D Raup Conus mesh (W=1.42, D=0.05, T=3.15)]; 2D shell silhouette IoU vs segmented Conus textile specimen = 0.8353 IoU (intersection/union) (reference 1.0, Conus textile OSU specimen 24399204286 (datasets/conus/conus_textile_specimen.jpg)) [pixel overlap between projected 3D Raup Conus mesh and segmented OSU Conus textile specimen silhouette (256x140 grid)]; Rule 30 white-tent chord-length CV (σ/μ) = 0.7075 CV (std/mean) (reference 0.6403, Conus textile OSU specimen dorsal white-tent segmentation (1,814 chords, CV=0.6403; exact geometric P(W=w)=2^{-w} theory CV=0.7071)) [coefficient of variation of horizontal unpigmented run lengths w on periodic mantle ring (230x370)] — Meinhardt-Klingler PDE CV = 1.1045 (vs close-up specimen ling_commons_010 CV = 1.1310); KS(Rule30, specimen) = 0.2623." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-conus-audit-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-conus-audit-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-conus-audit-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-conus-audit-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-conus-audit-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-conus-audit-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-6>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-conus-audit-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-7> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-conus-audit-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Wolfram (1984) Rule 30 & Meinhardt–Klingler (1987) Conus textile Pigmentation — MorphoEval overall 87.3/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Side-by-side generative reproduction and 1D space-time kymograph analysis of Wolfram (1984, 2002) Rule 30 cellular automata and Meinhardt & Klingler's (1987) activator-substrate-hormone reaction-diffusion PDE mapped onto a 3D Raup (1966) Conus textile shell mesh. Validated against OEIS A051023 (128/128 bits), Erica Jen's (1990) left-bijective inverse and diagonal period-doubling theorem (0 bit errors; dislocations at k = 0, 3, 8, 29, 400), and segmented OSU Conus textile specimen photography (H/W error 0.07%, 2D silhouette IoU 0.8353, white-tent chord CV 0.7069 vs specimen 0.6403). Overall 87.3/100 (faithfulness 86.4, reproducibility 89.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit fb234bc; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 89, Morphological realism / specimen match 84, Parameter expressivity 85, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 89, Reproducibility package 89. Output judged: conus_textile_rule30_comparison.png: rendered output of 1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py at fb234bc, image/png, 611089 B, 2640×1632 px, artifact_sha256 b204b836cd08e75a085169a5eb32b8069015a423668ea8a4963f251c1d130e41 (sha256 b204b836cd08e75a085169a5eb32b8069015a423668ea8a4963f251c1d130e41), spec_fingerprint 6baf9ffa515c0c89775df3b58f398571f7894e64d20534778dff610ad08bc313. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 6baf9ffa515c0c89775df3b58f398571f7894e64d20534778dff610ad08bc313; artifact_sha256: b204b836cd08e75a085169a5eb32b8069015a423668ea8a4963f251c1d130e41; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/conus/conus_textile_reference.json=dfcb500d87a39390...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Wolfram (1983, 1984, 2002) introduces elementary cellular automaton Rule 30 (a_{t+1,i} = a_{t,i-1} XOR (a_{t,i} OR a_{t,i+1})) as a discrete generative model of Conus textile tent pigmentation and poses the 2019 Rule 30 Prize Problems on the center column a_{t,0} (OEIS A051023) | Jen (1990) proves left-bijective spatial invertibility a_{t,i-1} = a_{t+1,i} XOR (a_{t,i} OR a_{t,i+1}) and the left-cone diagonal period-doubling cascade d_k(t+1) = d_{k-2}(t) XOR (d_{k-1}(t) OR d_k(t)) gated by all-zero synchronizing barriers d_{k-1} = 0 | Meinhardt & Klingler (1987) formulate a 1D mantle-edge activator-substrate-hormone reaction-diffusion PDE generating self-extinguishing pigment triangles and V-shaped lesion recovery wakes; reconstructed_in_script: Exact Boolean and GF(2) ANF Rule 30 evolution, 1024-step single-seed light-cone, Jen (1990) left-bijective reconstruction and k=0..414 diagonal period-doubling cascade (k = 0, 3, 8, 29, 400), directional Boolean damage-cone ensemble, Meinhardt-Klingler PDE kymograph and lesion scar simulation, and 3D Raup Conus shell projection validated against segmented OSU Conus textile photography; transfer_boundary: Cross-model 1D space-time defect-front kymograph comparison linking Rule 30 / Meinhardt mantle wakes to Zhang-Goldstein-Levin (2025) frozen-defect cell sorting and Cervera-Levin-Mafe (2021) bioelectric domain-wall propagation; does_not_claim: Infinite-horizon proof of the open 2019 Wolfram Rule 30 Prize Problems #1-#3 (verifies finite-horizon statistics through t = 1024 and exact diagonal periods through k = 414)." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30> ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Extend 3D Conus shell texture comparison from 2D orthographic silhouette IoU to unwrapped cylindrical UV registration against 360-degree photogrammetry of a single Conus textile shell.",
        "remediation needed: Include the 4-variable Meinhardt (1995) branched-travelling-wave system with explicit point-arrest hormone pulses for large triangular tent cascades." ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.73e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-conus-audit-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Wolfram (1984) Rule 30 & Meinhardt–Klingler (1987) Conus textile Pigmentation — Parameter expressivity: 85/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Contrasts Rule 30 against Rule 90 (linear XOR / Sierpinski negative control) and the continuous Meinhardt-Klingler PDE across intact growth and pinned mantle-edge lesion perturbations, sweeps diagonal index k across 415 left-cone diagonals and 25 damage-cone random seeds, and compares 1D space-time defect-front kymographs across four repository morphogenetic paradigms. Evidence: 1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py L425–L620: Pinned mantle-defect wakes (Rule 30 vs Meinhardt PDE) and cross-model kymograph front simulations <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fb234bc/1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py#L425-L620>; docs/media/conus_rule30_kymograph_defect_fronts.png (generated output, not in repo): 6-panel space-time kymograph & defect-front diagnostic figure — docs/media/conus_rule30_kymograph_defect_fronts.png: rendered output of 1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py at fb234bc, image/png, 509522 B, 2688×1664 px, artifact_sha256 61ea4422526b1008ce4c2245dc6f6a96a37da6547446583a8a0030fe50349b70 (sha256 61ea4422526b1008ce4c2245dc6f6a96a37da6547446583a8a0030fe50349b70), spec_fingerprint 6baf9ffa515c0c89775df3b58f398571f7894e64d20534778dff610ad08bc313." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

