    rdfs:comment "Directly segments two Wikimedia Commons Conus textile photographs (`stjohn_osu_24399204286`, CC BY 2.0, and `ling_commons_010`, Public Domain). The 3D Raup Conus mesh matches the OSU specimen's height-to-width ratio within 0.07% (1.8342 vs 1.8330) and achieves a 2D silhouette IoU of 0.8353. Rule 30 reproduces the full-shell white-tent chord-length CV (0.7069 vs specimen 0.6403, KS = 0.2389), while the Meinhardt-Klingler PDE matches the multi-scale close-up dorsal whorl dispersion (CV = 1.1050 vs 1.1310). Evidence: 1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py L837–L855: self_test(): 3D Raup mesh H/W, silhouette IoU, and chord-length KS/CV comparisons against segmented specimen <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fb234bc/1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py#L837-L855>; conus_textile_rule30_comparison.png (generated output, not in repo): Panel C silhouette IoU overlay (0.835) + segmented dorsal tents; Panel F white-chord CCDF tail comparison — conus_textile_rule30_comparison.png: rendered output of 1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py at fb234bc, image/png, 611089 B, 2640×1632 px, artifact_sha256 b204b836cd08e75a085169a5eb32b8069015a423668ea8a4963f251c1d130e41 (sha256 b204b836cd08e75a085169a5eb32b8069015a423668ea8a4963f251c1d130e41), spec_fingerprint 6baf9ffa515c0c89775df3b58f398571f7894e64d20534778dff610ad08bc313." ;
